  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1242 PM Sunday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...  A continuation of dry and seasonable conditions is \nexpected through the week, with above normal temperatures late this \nweek and weekend.\n\nA sub-tropical ridge will progress slowly eastward and across the \nSoutheast this week, then drift off the South Atlantic coast by next \nweekend. Largely seasonal temperatures will persist this upcoming \nweek with highs in the upper 60s to middle 70s. A moisture-starved \nbackdoor cold front will move in early Wednesday and result in a \nreinforcing shot of cool high pressure at least through Thursday.\n\nA warming trend is favored late this week and weekend, where \ntemperatures in the mid to upper 70s will be the norm. A few spots \ncould touch 80 degrees given the expected rise in low-level \nthicknesses.\n\nAs for rain chances, they are slim at best. Some ensemble systems \nare indicating a chance next Sunday to early next week with perhaps \na system building east from the TN valley. But then, other solutions \nkeep a ridge well in place and suppress precipitation. At this \nstage, we should stay dry through the end of October.",
